---
title: Finding
order: 1
description: Finding files and commands — find, locate, which, whereis, type
tags: [files, find, locate, updatedb, which, whereis, type]
---

Tools for locating files on disk and identifying command locations.

@text
find — search the filesystem in real time. Powerful but slower than indexed searches.

@code bash
# Find by name (case-sensitive)
find /var -name "*.log"

# Find by name (case-insensitive)
find /home -iname "*.jpg"

# Find by type: f=file, d=directory, l=symlink
find /etc -type f -name "*.conf"
find /usr -type d -name "bin"
find /usr -type l

# Find by size
find / -type f -size +100M          # larger than 100 MiB
find /tmp -type f -size -1k         # smaller than 1 KiB
find . -type f -size 0              # empty files

# Find by modification time
find /var/log -mtime -1             # modified in last 24 hours
find /tmp -mtime +30                # modified more than 30 days ago
find . -mmin -60                    # modified in last 60 minutes
find . -newer reference.txt         # modified after reference.txt

# Find by permissions
find / -perm -4000 -type f          # files with SUID bit
find / -perm -2000 -type f          # files with SGID bit
find . -perm 777                    # exact match: rwxrwxrwx
find . -perm -u+x -type f          # user-executable files

# Find by owner/group
find /home -user alice
find /var -group www-data

# Find empty files and directories
find . -empty

# Combine conditions
find /var -name "*.log" -size +10M -mtime -7
find . -name "*.tmp" -o -name "*.bak"         # OR
find . -not -name "*.go"                       # NOT
find . \( -name "*.c" -o -name "*.h" \) -type f

# Execute commands on results
find . -name "*.tmp" -delete
find . -name "*.log" -exec gzip {} \;
find . -type f -exec chmod 644 {} +
find . -name "*.sh" -exec grep -l "TODO" {} +

# Print with custom format
find . -type f -printf '%s %p\n'               # size and path
find . -type f -printf '%T@ %p\n' | sort -rn   # sort by mtime

# Limit search depth
find . -maxdepth 2 -name "*.go"
find . -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -type d         # immediate subdirs only

# Stay on one filesystem (don't cross mount boundaries)
find / -xdev -name "*.conf"

# Exclude directories
find . -path ./vendor -prune -o -name "*.go" -print
find . -not -path "./.git/*" -name "*.txt"

@text
locate / plocate — fast indexed file search. Queries a pre-built database.

@code bash
# Install plocate (modern replacement for mlocate)
sudo pacman -S plocate

# Update the database (run as root or via timer)
sudo updatedb

# Search for files
locate config.toml

# Case-insensitive search
locate -i readme

# Use glob patterns
locate "*.service"
locate "/etc/*.conf"

# Count matches instead of listing
locate -c "*.go"

# Show only files that still exist
locate -e "pattern"

# Limit number of results
locate -l 10 "*.log"

# Use regex
locate -r '/etc/.*\.conf$'

# Enable plocate timer for automatic updates (OpenRC cron or timer)
# Add to crontab: 0 * * * * /usr/bin/updatedb

@text
Identify command locations and types.

@code bash
# which — find executable in PATH
which python
which -a python              # show all matches in PATH

# whereis — locate binary, source, and man page
whereis gcc
whereis -b gcc               # binary only
whereis -m gcc               # man page only

# type — show how the shell interprets a command
type ls                      # alias, builtin, file, or function
type -a ls                   # all definitions
type -t ls                   # just the type word (alias/builtin/file/function/keyword)

# command -v — POSIX-portable alternative to which
command -v python

# Trace the full chain (alias -> function -> binary)
type ls                      # ls is aliased to 'ls --color=auto'
which ls                     # /usr/bin/ls
file /usr/bin/ls             # ELF 64-bit executable

# Find all commands matching a pattern
compgen -c | grep docker     # bash completion list
